A 2026 arXiv research paper by Kenan Zhang. In this note, the author recalls the Calderon-Zygmund theory on the unit ball and derives the weak (1,1) boundedness of the projection for ℋ \mathcal{H} -harmonic Bergman space. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification
42B20,31C05,46E22. Introduction

For
n\geqslant 2
, let
\mathbb{B}_{n}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{n}:|x|<1\}
be the unit ball and
\partial\mathbb{B}_{n}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{n}:|x|=1\}
be the unit sphere, where
|x|=(\sum_{i=1}^{n}|x_{i}|^{2})^{1/2}
is the standard Euclidean norm on
\mathbb{R}^{n}
. The hyperbolic ball is the unit ball
\mathbb{B}_{n}
equipped with the hyperbolic metric

ds^{2}=\frac{4}{(1-|x|^{2})^{2}}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}dx_{i}^{2}.

A 2025 arXiv research paper by Nika Mlinarič Hribar. Abstract

This study investigates the impact of wind velocity averaging on Dynamic Thermal Rating (DTR) calculations. It is based on a high-temporal-resolution (
1\text{\,}\mathrm{s}
) wind measurements obtained from a transmission line in Slovenia, Europe. Wind speed and direction variability are analysed, and two averaging methods, namely vector averaging, where velocity is averaged as vector, and hybrid averaging, where speed is averaged as scalar, are employed. DTR calculations are performed on both high-resolution data and averaged data (averaging window
5\text{\,}\mathrm{min}
).
